{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars","id":996711,"title":"Do we know anything new about Lunars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-01T11:37:34-07:00","id":996711,"title":"Do we know anything new about Lunars?","content":"I've been poking around a bit on this board trying to find information about Lunars, (Which, looking at recent progress, I expect to see in late 2023). Have we heard anything as of late? I can't find too much to satisfy my curiosity outside of the core book and this site: <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars</a> (which sadly hasn't been kept up after the release of the core book). What else is there? (is there a fan version that is popular?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:15:21-07:00","id":996737,"title":"","content":"It's not really something new specifically, but there was a discussion on RPG.Net a couple of months ago in which Holden reaffirmed the idea of Lunars who have nothing to do with fighting against the Realm, not only as acceptable but as fully accommodated by the basic concept of Lunars.<br /> <br /> They're not really my cup of tea, but the Terrible or Terrifying or whatever Argent Witches were a fan made concept of Lunars that were rather elaborately detailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:27:08-07:00","id":996749,"title":"","content":"Things have gone real quiet in general since the Core dropped. They're working on Arms, working on Dragon-Blooded, working on The Realm, etc. Getting backer stuff out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:49:39-07:00","id":996853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=996749#post996749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things have gone real quiet in general since the Core dropped. They're working on Arms, working on Dragon-Blooded, working on The Realm, etc. Getting backer stuff out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like Holden is still semi-active in the RPGnet exalted threads, but yeah it has otherwise been pretty quiet on all exalted fronts. They probably still lurk here though, I can't imagine they have been ignoring the forum since March.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:56:08-07:00","id":996859,"title":"","content":"I asked John a question about whether Lunars can turn into Spirits in 3e on Twitter, but he never replied.<br /> <br /> I understand not wanting to answer that question though. I kind of just want to put it to bed so I can stop feeling bad about carving out charms that do that from the conversion I've been using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:11:35-07:00","id":996865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=996859#post996859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked John a question about whether Lunars can turn into Spirits in 3e on Twitter, but he never replied.<br /> <br /> I understand not wanting to answer that question though. I kind of just want to put it to bed so I can stop feeling bad about carving out charms that do that from the conversion I've been using.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like somewhere it was said that that taking on the forms of spirits probably wasn't going to be in their wheelhouse anymore, just people and animals. But I have no idea where or how long ago this impression is coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:58:48-07:00","id":996888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=996865#post996865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like somewhere it was said that that taking on the forms of spirits probably wasn't going to be in their wheelhouse anymore, just people and animals. But I have no idea where or how long ago this impression is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure your recollection is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T02:52:01-07:00","id":997063,"title":"","content":"I remember that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T02:58:42-07:00","id":997064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=996865#post996865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel like somewhere it was said that that taking on the forms of spirits probably wasn't going to be in their wheelhouse anymore, just people and animals. But I have no idea where or how long ago this impression is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I like that. I mean, not out of the box, obviously, but a Lunar shapeshifter, one optomized for it, should be the kind of thing that can slip into Yu-Shan or Malfas, which is pretty hard to do if you're playing glorified squirrel shapechanger. I'll wait, but past versions of Lunars leave me a little nervous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T03:30:46-07:00","id":997068,"title":"","content":"That doesn't require literally turning into demons - it's not like it's hard to shapeshift into an ape and then dye your fur red. It's not like the demons can peek at your character sheet and say, &quot;Hey! This guy doesn't have Principle of Motion! Get 'im!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:43:45-07:00","id":997132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=997068#post997068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't require literally turning into demons - it's not like it's hard to shapeshift into an ape and then dye your fur red. It's not like the demons can peek at your character sheet and say, &amp;quot;Hey! This guy doesn't have Principle of Motion! Get 'im!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair most apes lack back-spikes- wait if they can still take wyld-mutant forms this is a nonissue. Then it just requires patience and experimentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:49:05-07:00","id":997135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars#post996711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been poking around a bit on this board trying to find information about Lunars, (Which, looking at recent progress, I expect to see in late 2023). Have we heard anything as of late? I can't find too much to satisfy my curiosity outside of the core book and this site: <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars</a> (which sadly hasn't been kept up after the release of the core book). What else is there? (is there a fan version that is popular?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I could call any of 'em &quot;popular,&quot; but there are some fan conversions to 3e floating around.<br /> <br /> For instance:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:45:41-07:00","id":997165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=997132#post997132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to be fair most apes lack back-spikes\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Spikes can also be part of the disguise. <br /> <br /> Really, there's such a bevy of demonic shapes out there that I have a hard time believing that a clever Lunar with only human and animal shapes and moderate skill at disguise and deception couldn't convince at least <i>some</i> demons that he is a fellow demon. <br /> <br /> The thing to watch out for would be staying ineligible for uses of Measure the Wind in demons who might have reason to <i>suspect</i> you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-02-2016, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:55:04-07:00","id":997173,"title":"","content":"And then of course there's Hybrid Body Rearrangement. Which may not be there in 3rd ed, but I do think it's likely that Lunars will have some way to merge multiple shapes, especially with what they were saying about Chimera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:15:28-07:00","id":997187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=997064#post997064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I like that. I mean, not out of the box, obviously, but a Lunar shapeshifter, one optomized for it, should be the kind of thing that can slip into Yu-Shan or Malfas, which is pretty hard to do if you're playing glorified squirrel shapechanger. I'll wait, but past versions of Lunars leave me a little nervous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be open to them having charms to superficially mimic spirits, just take their physical shape, but not their powers. In the same vein as it probably being ok for them to have charms that let them take on another person's appearance in a limited way even if they haven't taken their hearts blood. But in both these cases you should definitely have to go through some extra effort to assume the form and be limited in how reliable or long lasting it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:07:33-07:00","id":997215,"title":"","content":"I'd also point out, it's unlikely demons are just going to kill a Lunar for showing up in Malfeas. Those not bound are a special resource. A Lunar has the potential to summon both 1st and 2nd Circle demons into Creation. That's not something you squander just to kill a random Exalt. Simply put, any Exalt that shows up in Malfeas should initially be viewed as a potential resource by the demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:24:44-07:00","id":997262,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to hear about other realm's opinions on Lunars in the new edition. They're supposed to be a bigger part of the setting now, and all we hear about in past editions is what Ghosts, Gods, and Demons think of Solars, Abyssals, Infernals, and sometimes Dragon-Blooded. Oh and Sids I guess. But how do Ghosts feel about Lunars? What about heaven? What about Hell? They're the odd-ducks out for a lot of these settings and I'd love to hear them considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:26:07-07:00","id":997304,"title":"","content":"I think the idea that a viable alternative to turning into a blood ape is turning into a regular ape and dressing it up to look like a blood ape is a bit silly.<br /> <br /> I'd point out that the capacity to turn into a small bird or rodent is probably a good way to infiltrate almost anywhere, regardless of the existing presence of such animals. Just being small and mobile is a big help.<br /> <br /> So it leads into the question of whether or not a Lunar should be specifically able to infiltrate somewhere like Yu-Shan by pretending to be one of its native inhabitants. To which I say that I would have to wait and see what the full range of Lunar capabilities is, but would provisionally suggest that they don't strictly need to be universal infiltration experts of that type.<br /> <br /> The whole thing about Lunars turning into spirits (or ghosts) emerged out of a question of whether or not they would automatically partake in the powers of such things, which was pointed out to create a lot of complications.<br /> <br /> If you say that Lunars automatically gain any powers for a thing that they've turned into, then you're likely creating an overwhelming incentive for Lunars to collect the forms of spirits, as well as kind of drowning out some of the familiar Lunar aesthetic.<br /> <br /> If they don't, then it's a lot like the transformation is a shallow disguise, because it can't back itself up in significant ways.<br /> <br /> I considered there was a possibility in something like the powers Solars have been given to acquire Charms outside of the Eclipse Anima, but I currently think those may not really be able to keep up with the possibility of Lunars having multiple forms of things like spirits.<br /> <br /> A lot of it seems like a mess, and the kind of thing that the idea of Lunar shapeshifting extending to being able to infiltrate places such as Yu-Shan and Malfeas with a great deal of varietymight be worth sacrificing to avoid.<br /> <br /> I suppose the biggest other thing to consider is what might come of the powers of Lunars around and outside of shapeshifting. For instance, the question of whether or not something like shapeshifting renders disguise as unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I find it highly likely that Lunars will have Charms in things like Strength or Dexterity to enhance their ability to fight, rather than universally being required to fall back upon turning into a large dinosaur, so perhaps similar principles will apply.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I think it's all right for them to operate differently in different theaters; for something like a long-term plan to imitate the life of another to be a lot more viable with humans in Creation than it is with gods in Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:08:04-07:00","id":997326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=997304#post997304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea that a viable alternative to turning into a blood ape is turning into a regular ape and dressing it up to look like a blood ape is a bit silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I was only being about ~25% serious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, for that matter, while they're far from plentiful, there <i>are</i> humans in Malfeas, and they're largely not killed on sight. Often it's because they're the property of someone else, or are otherwise provided some sort of protection. It may not be very dignified, but a Lunar could always take the place of an influential demon's mortal consort.<br /> <br /> Also, there are almost certainly squirrels in the Celestial City. A number of gods have &quot;gardens&quot; on their palatial estates - some of which will be the size of Rhode Island.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-02-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T00:28:50-07:00","id":998637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=997304#post997304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you say that Lunars automatically gain any powers for a thing that they've turned into, then you're likely creating an overwhelming incentive for Lunars to collect the forms of spirits, as well as kind of drowning out some of the familiar Lunar aesthetic.<br /> <br /> If they don't, then it's a lot like the transformation is a shallow disguise, because it can't back itself up in significant ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall if it was ink monkey's, fan material or published in the glories, but there was a charm that allowed a Lunar to &quot;reskin&quot; his or her charms to appear to outside viewers to look like they were native to whatever form he was wearing. That might be a way to avoid the: get all the power, you become uber lunar, don't get the, you become easily detected lunar. <br /> <br /> Or you could use the solar &quot;secret identity&quot; charms as a baseline for creating entirely new personas that have charms but also have a higher buyin. I mean, I have <i>no</i> problem with the idea that impersonating a second circle demon and waltzing into Malfas is the sort of thing that only very, very experienced lunars can pull off. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:26:57-07:00","id":998832,"title":"","content":"I got the sense that ditching the spirit shapeshifting is part of an effort to move the Lunars away from just being the Shapeshifting Exalted, so that everything shapeshifting ever doesn't have to be the Lunars only thing.<br /> <br /> I think it might help make their concept a bit more distinct, which would be cool. Shapeshifting into everything ever feels kind of boring to me, to be honest.<br /> <br /> EDIT: to clarify, I think a concept like Alex Mercer is really cool and I would want to make a character like that, I just would prefer if it were its own thing as opposed to having to force that into the Lunar Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 11-05-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:55:42-07:00","id":998991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=998637#post998637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't recall if it was ink monkey's, fan material or published in the glories, but there was a charm that allowed a Lunar to &quot;reskin&quot; his or her charms to appear to outside viewers to look like they were native to whatever form he was wearing. That might be a way to avoid the: get all the power, you become uber lunar, don't get the, you become easily detected lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe thing that brought up the comparison was the matter of ghosts, and the presumed capacity to walk through walls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:15:59-07:00","id":999027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=998991#post998991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe thing that brought up the comparison was the matter of ghosts, and the presumed capacity to walk through walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would feel absolutely guiltless giving this to a NPC Lunar, since those who survived the flight into the wyld surely underwent many strange transformations, and many have worked countless bizarre sorcerous workings on their bodies. The upside to having no splatbook is that nothing really stops you from the outer limits of your imagination, not even the informal limitations suggested by the charmsets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:40:13-07:00","id":999042,"title":"","content":"Err, I'd be a little cautious about that in my game-- at some point the lunars are getting their splatbook and few things annoy my players more than finding out that X awesome power is an NPC only power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:44:11-07:00","id":999046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999042#post999042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err, I'd be a little cautious about that in my game-- at some point the lunars are getting their splatbook and few things annoy my players more than finding out that X awesome power is an NPC only power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're doing that after the book is released, sure. But making shit up and then quietly trimming what needs to be trimmed is a time-honored tradition within Exalted <i>canon</i>. Remember the Storyteller Guide, which had a bunch of &quot;preview&quot; charms for unreleased Exalt types, all of which were at least a little bit busted? Well, maybe not. It's been ten years. Jesus. It's been ten years!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:45:12-07:00","id":999062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999027#post999027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would feel absolutely guiltless giving this to a NPC Lunar, <b>since those who survived the flight into the wyld surely underwent many strange transformations</b>, and many have worked countless bizarre sorcerous workings on their bodies. The upside to having no splatbook is that nothing really stops you from the outer limits of your imagination, not even the informal limitations suggested by the charmsets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much in this edition, since they didn't really flee too far into the lands of chaos (and they don't really hang out there, either, since their interest is in Creation). The Wyld also didn't break their castes; the upheaval of the Solars being slain and banished from the cosmos did.<br /> <br /> As for dematerializing, I think that they might have an in-Exalt Charm for it. Air-Body Style can fit within the confines of a shamanic theme, and the root splat from the WoD could go from physical to spirit in form and back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:53:02-08:00","id":999199,"title":"","content":"Actually, the Lunars broke <i>their own</i> castes in Ex3 according to Dev commentary, though it <i>was</i> a product of the Usurpation. It was less &quot;Well, Solars are dead. Wait, what happened to the Waxing and Waning Moons?&quot;, and more &quot;Well, Solars are dead. Our entire setup needs to change if we are to survive.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:57:34-08:00","id":999276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=998991#post998991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe thing that brought up the comparison was the matter of ghosts, and the presumed capacity to walk through walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the same conversation where John compared Lunar shapeshifting-into-a-ghost to a person throwing a bedsheet over his head.<br /> <br /> It was a weird and confusing conversation. (Edit: from around <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?745142-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt2-(Hidden-Meaning-Behind-Veiled-Words-Style)&amp;p=18725374#post18725374\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:20:19-08:00","id":999455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999276#post999276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the same conversation where John compared Lunar shapeshifting-into-a-ghost to a person throwing a bedsheet over his head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn other words, a shallow disguise that was incapable of backing itself up in a significant way.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a weird and confusing conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOhhhhhhh I wish you hadn't said that.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be inappropriate for me to talk about my opinion of how some people reacted in that conversation, and yet not only is it the kind of line that will twist its way around inside of my head, but it's something that I feel as though to leave unaddressed would be a kind of tacit agreement.<br /> <br /> \u200bSuffice to say that my opinion is counter to this one, just so that it doesn't get to be the only word on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T20:16:19-08:00","id":999549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999455#post999455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn other words, a shallow disguise that was incapable of backing itself up in a significant way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, precisely. And &quot;a shallow disguise incapable of backing itself up&quot; is not how I typically think of Lunar shapeshifting - hence the confusion.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bOhhhhhhh I wish you hadn't said that.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be inappropriate for me to talk about my opinion of how some people reacted in that conversation, </div> </div> </div>C'mon, dude. If you disagree, by all means say so, but I would appreciate it if we did not do a &quot;Can't-say-it-but-I-sure-can-hint&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> (I thought it was a pretty good thread - though, again, I found John's posts a bit unclear. Mostly civil, broadly informative; probably relevant to the OP, in any event.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-06-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T21:47:59-08:00","id":999572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999549#post999549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, precisely. And &quot;a shallow disguise incapable of backing itself up&quot; is not how I typically think of Lunar shapeshifting - hence the confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one logical outcome, predicated on Lunars being too broad in their shapeshifting, is that their capability to turn into ghosts and such should be improved. The other is that Lunars shouldn't turn into ghosts, which is probably the one we're getting. Not that it's really a big impediment, seeing as how I'm betting that Lunars will probably still be able to dematerialize, but the whole &quot;infiltrator on par with T-1000&quot; part of the Lunars was massively overplayed in second edition, so some blowback is expected, likely up until the Lunars' complementary splats are revealed/released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:02:49-08:00","id":999658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999549#post999549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, precisely. And &quot;a shallow disguise incapable of backing itself up&quot; is not how I typically think of Lunar shapeshifting - hence the confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! That's not how Lunar shapeshifting should work!<br /> <br /> \u200bSo it should not be the case that Lunars assume the form of ghosts while being unable to walk through walls!<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the same time that it would be overpowered or disproportionately incentivized if they <i>did</i> get to walk through walls just by eating a ghost.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow was this confusing?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">C'mon, dude. If you disagree, by all means say so, but I would appreciate it if we did not do a &quot;Can't-say-it-but-I-sure-can-hint&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI know, and I hate that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the problem is that I find it particularly difficult to state disagreement with something like confusion, because that's an extremely subjective experience. At the same time, I'm perplexed about how it was confusing, but fear that to say so is to cast aspersions on other people.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, for the sake of clarity, I'm putting that out there now, and if it is crossing a line then I shall accept it and apologize.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut still present the alternative viewpoint in the hopes that people would not run away with the assumption that the posts themselves were completely impenetrable.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:49:20-08:00","id":999668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999658#post999658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI know, and I hate that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the problem is that I find it particularly difficult to state disagreement with something like confusion, because that's an extremely subjective experience. At the same time, I'm perplexed about how it was confusing, but fear that to say so is to cast aspersions on other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... okay, here: let's try a straightforward statement of <i>where I think that conversation ended up:</i><br /> <br /> &quot;I think it's inappropriate for Lunars to be able to gain the shape of ghosts without also gaining all of a ghost's various supernatural whatsits, including but not limited to the ability to be naturally immaterial. I think similar problems exist for other kinds of spirit or supernatural thing, and I think it's kind of dumb for Lunars to be able to turn into plants or terrain features or emotions or odder things. Thus, my expectation at this time is that, when I write Lunars, they'll only be able to <i>actually turn into</i> animals and people, though they'll probably have some sort of disguise magic <i>a la </i>Solar Larceny to <i>appear</i> to be lots of other things.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I <i>like</i> that position, but I at least understand what it is. John prefers, I think, a very... poetic, maybe?... explanation style; it sounds like that clicks well for you, but that's not true of everyone, and his posts about bedsheet ghosts and Swiss army knives and Lunars with the full Solar Charmset didn't help me much, there. Any internet conversation already has ambiguities of &quot;Is my tone being read correctly?&quot; and &quot;Is the person I'm asking a question of understanding the question?&quot; before we get to &quot;What am I to make of his answer?&quot; - and as I'd prefer not to assume that my conversation partner has made an implication that he actually didn't intend, all of that makes me more hesitant to try to jump to conclusions about what's being meant.<br /> <br /> Hence, a confusing conversation. Does that make better sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:15:40-08:00","id":999672,"title":"","content":"New to that discussion, but the Swiss Army knife analogy was not particularly confusing to me.<br /> <br /> A Swiss Army knife has a number of tools in it. For all sorts of practical, aesthetic, and logical reasons, a motorcycle cannot number among those tools. If its design <i>did</i> somehow incorporate a motorcycle, the &quot;motorcycle&quot; part would overwhelm the &quot;knife&quot; part that no one would be thinking of it as a &quot;knife&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> In this analogy, the Lunar is the knife, turning into animals and humans represents the screwdriver, corkscrew, toothbrush, et cetera., and turning into spirits represents people hamfistedly attempting to graft a motorcycle onto a Swiss Army knife.<br /> <br /> The bedsheets thing was a different analogy, but not remotely more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:23:11-08:00","id":999674,"title":"","content":"I'm not interested in relitigating the conversation, here; Isator asked why I/some people found it confusing, and I'm making a good-faith effort to answer that question.<br /> <br /> If you find it perfectly clear on reading it now, with the whole conversation already finished, great! But let's not conflate <i>difficult analogies </i>with <i>caution in assuming unstated conclusions.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 11-07-2016, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:30:35-08:00","id":999675,"title":"","content":"The conclusion was pretty stated: there's no plan for Lunars to turn into spirits, let alone assume their traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:47:05-08:00","id":999686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/996711-do-we-know-anything-new-about-lunars?p=999675#post999675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conclusion was pretty stated: there's no plan for Lunars to turn into spirits, let alone assume their traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. If that's <i>prima facie</i> clear to you, reading those first couple of posts, then good deal; as I say, it's a conversation style that seems to really click with some people, and less so with others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}